# StudentStack — Cursor Rules (strict)

## Brand & UI/UX
- Visual language: extreme modern roundness (large border radii), bubbly rounded sans-serif typography, soft and vibrant pastels, thick drop shadows, playful bouncy hover animations (reference: Duolingo, Kalshi energy).
- Interactions: prefer `motion` / CSS transitions with subtle scale and shadow on hover; avoid flat static panels without feedback.

## Icons
- Never use generic placeholder icons, emoji-as-icons for UI chrome, or “AI JSON” / stock robot icons.
- Use **Lucide React** (or other curated SVG icon libraries) or intentional **CSS shapes** only.

## Product & Content Boundaries
- **StudentStack** is a student-led org for parents of high schoolers and student learners.
- **Free daily newsletter** for parents: keep the hero description vague (social traffic already knows the pitch). No long climate encyclopedias above the fold.
- **Monetization** on the public site: educational **courses** and **certifications** (waitlist / inquire / enroll framing). Prefer novel course concepts; frame major/background benefits tastefully (no stereotypes, no “guaranteed admissions”).
- Certification partners may be placeholder / fictional institutes for now. Do not claim real university degrees, official university seals, or accredited credentials you do not have.
- Do **not** implement or reference: “StudentStack Elite,” 24/7 concierge paid peer support, or hard portal upsells as the primary CTA.
- The “college student team” presentation is a **branding layer**; keep Meet-the-Team style optics.

## Engineering defaults
- App is Next.js at the repo root (`package.json` in `/`). Do not introduce unrelated frameworks or large refactors unless explicitly requested.
